V. Which of the following customary units could we use?\n\nI. $\\textrm{yd}$\n\nII. $\\textrm{ft}$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{lb}$" :question/worked-solution "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\textrm{ton}$ |\n| Pound | $\\textrm{lb}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\textrm{oz}$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of mass is $\\textrm{lb}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198069 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e0296c8-9ada-5097-a967-f10fc498a9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Stating Mass Conversions in Customary Units"}] :question/id #uuid "16c47009-d38d-5957-bc2d-525483e18161" :question/math-academy-id "e-12517" :question/problem "An american bison has a mass of $1\\,\\textrm{ton}.$ What is this mass in pounds?" :question/worked-solution "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\textrm{ton}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{ton} = 2,000\\,\\textrm{lb}$ |\n| Pound | $\\textrm{lb}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{lb} = 16\\,\\textrm{oz}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\textrm{oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\textrm{ton}$ is equivalent to $2,000\\,\\textrm{lb}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e01d9e5b-d4e5-5e84-84c5-33f6678b53ee" :knowledge-point/title "Stating Mass Conversions in Metric Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "145bf05e-e6d7-5946-85aa-37adc9c46ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1\\,\\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431547} {:answer/id #uuid "6c392e3c-f095-51d9-a302-8b66997cad2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100\\,\\text{g}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431591} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbaf0c0-2434-5290-b202-0e738d9a2ade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498